    Note:
        Mochi will select the most appropriate collider type based on the actor's
        shape and type: - Implicit sphere shapes: :class:`SPHERE
        <superdex.physics.ColliderType>` - Implicit plane shapes: :class:`PLANE
        <superdex.physics.ColliderType>` - Mesh shapes on volumetric actors (e.g.,
        rigid, soft): :class:`SDF <superdex.physics.ColliderType>` - Shell and rod
        actors: :class:`POINT_CLOUD <superdex.physics.ColliderType>`

    Note:
        If Auto is set on an actor, a valid collider type will be assigned even if
        the shape's default collider type is :class:`NONE
        <superdex.physics.ColliderType>`. If you want :class:`NONE
        <superdex.physics.ColliderType>`, set :class:`NONE
        <superdex.physics.ColliderType>` explicitly as your collider type.

    Note:
        After initialization, :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_collider_type` will
        return the selected type, not :class:`AUTO <superdex.physics.ColliderType>`.
    """
    SPHERE: ColliderType
