    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric`
    """
    shape: ShapeHandle
    """Shape handle defining the actor's geometry and other metadata.

    Note:
        A shape can be shared by multiple actors, even actors in different scenes.

    Note:
        Dynamic rigid actors require a shape with a surface mesh.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ShapeHandle`,
        :func:`~superdex.physics.load_shape_from_file`
    """
    world_from_local: TransformRT
    """Initial rotation and translation of the actor's local frame with respect to
    world frame.

    Note:
        The actor's center of mass may be located elsewhere, since it is not
        necessarily at the origin of the actor's local coordinate frame.

    See Also:
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.center_of_mass`
    """
    collider_type: ColliderType
    """Collision detection geometry.

    Note:
        Determines how OTHER actors detect contact with this actor. It does not
        affect how this actor detects contact with other actors.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ColliderType`
    """
    is_static: bool
    """If true, actor will be static (fixed in space). If false, actor will be dynamic.
    """
    contact: ContactParams
    """Contact mechanics parameters.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ContactParams`
    """
    sdf: GridSdfParams
    """Parameters used to construct a grid-based Signed Distance Field (SDF) if the
    shape doesn't already have one.

    Note:
        Ignored if :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.collider_type` is not
        :class:`SDF <superdex.physics.ColliderType>`.

    Note:
        Ignored if the shape already has a grid-based SDF.
    """
    has_gravity: bool
    """If true, actor is affected by gravity.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.set_gravity`
    """
    density: Optional[float]
    """Uniform density [kg/m³] of the actor. Must be positive if provided.

    Note:
        Setting both density and mass is not recommended. If both are set, mass
        takes precedence and density is ignored.

    Note:
        If only density is set, mass is computed automatically from volume.

    Note:
        If neither is set, :const:`~superdex.physics.DEFAULT_DENSITY` is used.

    See Also:
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.mass`
    """
    mass: Optional[float]
    """Total mass [kg] of the actor. Must be positive if provided.

    Note:
        Setting both mass and density is not recommended. If both are set, mass
        takes precedence and density is ignored.

    Note:
        If only mass is set, density is computed automatically from volume.

    See Also:
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.density`
    """
    @property
    def center_of_mass(self) -> Optional[Real3]:
        """Position [m] of the center of mass in the actor's local frame.

        Note:
            If not set, computed automatically from geometry.

        Note:
            Usually combined with explicit momentOfInertia.

        See Also:
            :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.moment_of_inertia`
        """
    @center_of_mass.setter
    def center_of_mass(self, value: Optional[Real3Like]) -> None: ...
    @property
    def moment_of_inertia(self) -> Optional[Real6]:
        """Moment of inertia tensor [kg·m²] at the center of mass in the actor's local
        frame.

        Stored as [ixx, ixy, ixz, iyy, iyz, izz] using negative tensor notation:

        ::

                 [ixx, ixy, ixz]   [ +∫(y²+z²)dm,  -∫(xy)dm,    -∫(xz)dm    ]
             I = [ixy, iyy, iyz] = [ -∫(xy)dm,     +∫(x²+z²)dm, -∫(yz)dm    ]
                 [ixz, iyz, izz]   [ -∫(xz)dm,     -∫(yz)dm,    +∫(x²+y²)dm ]

        Note:
            Uses negative tensor notation consistent with e.g. robotics URDF files.

        Note:
            Many CAD tools (e.g., Solidworks) use positive tensor notation requiring
            negation of off-diagonal terms. See
            https://www.mathworks.com/help/sm/ug/specify-custom-inertia.html.

        Note:
            Must be finite. A finite but physically invalid tensor (negative principal
            moments or one violating the triangle inequality) is accepted with a
            warning, not rejected.

        Note:
            If not set, computed automatically from geometry and density.

        Note:
            Usually combined with explicit centerOfMass.

        See Also:
            :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.center_of_mass`
        """
    @moment_of_inertia.setter
    def moment_of_inertia(self, value: Optional[Real6Like]) -> None: ...
    boundary_element_type: ActorBoundaryElementType
    """Finite element type for boundary discretization.

    Note:
        Affects accuracy and performance of contact and boundary integrals.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ActorBoundaryElementType`
    """
    boundary_subsampling: Optional[BoundarySubsamplingParams]
    """Optional subsampling for boundary integrals such as contact.

    Note:
        Reduces computational cost by using fewer sample points.

    Note:
        For best performance, combine subsampling with
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams.boundary_element_type` =
        :class:`P1Q1 <superdex.physics.ActorBoundaryElementType>`.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.BoundarySubsamplingParams`
    """
    @property
    def linear_velocity(self) -> Optional[Real3]:
        """Optional initial linear velocity of the center of mass in world frame [m/s],
        zero otherwise.

        Note:
            Not valid for static rigid actors or articulated links.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_linear_velocity`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_velocity`
        """
    @linear_velocity.setter
    def linear_velocity(self, value: Optional[Real3Like]) -> None: ...
    @property
    def angular_velocity(self) -> Optional[Real3]:
        """Optional initial angular velocity in world frame [rad/s], zero otherwise.

        Note:
            Not valid for static rigid actors or articulated links.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_angular_velocity`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_velocity`
        """
    @angular_velocity.setter
    def angular_velocity(self, value: Optional[Real3Like]) -> None: ...
    @overload
    def __init__(self) -> None: ...
    @overload
    def __init__(
        self,
        name: str = ...,
        layer: str = ...,
        shape: ShapeHandle = ...,
        world_from_local: TransformRT = ...,
        collider_type: ColliderType | int = ...,
        is_static: bool = ...,
        contact: ContactParams = ...,
        sdf: GridSdfParams = ...,
        has_gravity: bool = ...,
        density: Optional[float] = ...,
        mass: Optional[float] = ...,
        center_of_mass: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
        moment_of_inertia: Optional[Real6Like] = ...,
        boundary_element_type: ActorBoundaryElementType | int = ...,
        boundary_subsampling: Optional[BoundarySubsamplingParams] = ...,
        linear_velocity: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
        angular_velocity: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
    ) -> None: ...
    def __eq__(self, other: object) -> bool: ...
    def __ne__(self, other: object) -> bool: ...

class SoftActorParams:
    """Parameters to create a soft deformable actor.

    Soft actors are volumetric deformable bodies simulated using the Finite Element
    Method (FEM).

    Note:
        Soft actors created via :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.create_soft_actor`
        act as colliding actors via their own surface sample points but not as
        colliders. To create a soft actor with a collider, use
        :func:`~superdex.physics.experimental.create_soft_actor` with an explicit
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.experimental.ExperimentalSoftActorParams.collider_type`.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.create_soft_actor`,
        :func:`~superdex.physics.experimental.create_soft_actor`,
        :class:`~superdex.physics.experimental.ExperimentalSoftActorParams`
    """
    name: str
    """Optional actor name. Uniqueness of names is not enforced.

    Note:
        When used in :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.soft_params`,
        this is interpreted as a nested soft local name. See
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.soft_params` for additional
        requirements and defaulting behavior.
    """
    layer: str
    """Contact layer name for filtering contacts between actors.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric`
    """
    world_from_local: TransformRT
    """Initial rotation and translation of the actor's local frame with respect to
    world frame.

    Note:
        When this struct is used as an entry of
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.soft_params`, this transform
        must be identity. The soft actor's shape must be defined directly in the
        reference frame of the articulated actor (see
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.skeleton_params`). The
        soft-skinned actor's placement in the scene world is provided by
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams.world_from_root` in
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.skeleton_params`.
    """
    shape: ShapeHandle
    """Shape handle defining the actor's geometry and other metadata.

    Note:
        Must be a TetrahedralMeshShape for soft actors.

    Note:
        A shape can be shared by multiple actors, even actors in different scenes.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ShapeHandle`,
        :func:`~superdex.physics.load_shape_from_file`
    """
    material: SoftMaterialParams
    """Uniform material properties.

    Note:
        If the shape contains per-element material data of the same
        :class:`~superdex.physics.SoftMaterialType`, the per-element values from the
        shape take precedence over and replace these uniform values. If the shape's
        per-element material type differs, these uniform values are used instead.

    Note:
        The actor uses a single PSD strategy for all elements. By default it is the
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.material`\\'s PSD strategy. If the
        shape supplies per-element material data of a matching
        :class:`~superdex.physics.SoftMaterialType` whose
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.PerElementSoftMaterialData.psd_strategy` is
        specified (i.e. not :class:`MATERIAL_DEFAULT
        <superdex.physics.MaterialPsdStrategy>`), that value takes precedence. If
        the :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.material`\\'s PSD strategy is
        also specified, the two must be equal.

    Note:
        Non-uniform material properties can also be applied after the actor is
        created. See experimental::SetSoftMaterialParamsField.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_soft_material_params`,
        :func:`~superdex.physics.experimental.set_soft_material_params_field`
    """
    contact: ContactParams
    """Contact mechanics parameters.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ContactParams`
    """
    has_gravity: bool
    """If true, actor is affected by gravity.

    Note:
        Unless the soft actor is part of a soft-skinned actor
        (:attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.soft_params`), at least one
        of :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_gravity`,
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_inertia` or
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_stress` must be enabled.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.set_gravity`
    """
    has_inertia: bool
    """If true, actor is affected by inertial forces.

    Note:
        Disable for quasi-static simulations.

    Note:
        Unless the soft actor is part of a soft-skinned actor
        (:attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.soft_params`), at least one
        of :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_gravity`,
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_inertia` or
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_stress` must be enabled.
    """
    has_stress: bool
    """If true, actor is affected by internal stress/strain forces.

    Note:
        Unless the soft actor is part of a soft-skinned actor
        (:attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.soft_params`), at least one
        of :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_gravity`,
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_inertia` or
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftActorParams.has_stress` must be enabled.
    """
    boundary_element_type: ActorBoundaryElementType
    """Finite element type for boundary discretization.

    Note:
        Affects accuracy and performance of contact and boundary integrals.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ActorBoundaryElementType`
    """
    @overload
    def __init__(self) -> None: ...
    @overload
    def __init__(
        self,
        name: str = ...,
        layer: str = ...,
        world_from_local: TransformRT = ...,
        shape: ShapeHandle = ...,
        material: SoftMaterialParams = ...,
        contact: ContactParams = ...,
        has_gravity: bool = ...,
        has_inertia: bool = ...,
        has_stress: bool = ...,
        boundary_element_type: ActorBoundaryElementType | int = ...,
    ) -> None: ...
    def __eq__(self, other: object) -> bool: ...
    def __ne__(self, other: object) -> bool: ...

class ArticulatedJointParams:
    """Parameters describing a single joint within an articulated actor.

    Each joint connects a link to its parent in the kinematic tree. Joints are
    referenced positionally — the i-th entry of
    :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams.joints` corresponds to the joint
    connecting the i-th link to its parent. Cycle-closing joints are declared
    separately via :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams.cycles`.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams`,
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedLinkParams`,
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType`
    """
    name: str
    """Joint name. Must be unique among joints of the same articulated actor.

    Note:
        If left empty, a unique default name (e.g., "joint_0", "joint_1", ...) is
        assigned automatically.
    """
    type: ArticulatedJointType
    """Joint type.

    Note:
        Default :class:`INVALID <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` is a
        sentinel. The user must overwrite it.

    Note:
        :class:`CYCLE <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` is reserved for
        cycle-closing joints. Use
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams.cycles` for cycle joints.

    Note:
        Static links can be modeled using a :class:`HARD
        <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` joint whose parent is either -1 or
        another static link.
    """
    parent_link_from_joint: TransformRT
    """Rotation and translation of the joint with respect to the parent link."""
    @property
    def axis(self) -> Real3:
        """Local axis of motion for the joint, in the joint's local frame.

        Note:
            Only used for :class:`PRISMATIC <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` and
            :class:`REVOLUTE <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` joints. Ignored
            (and reset to zero) for other joint types.

        Note:
            For Prismatic/Revolute joints, must be non-zero and finite. The vector is
            automatically normalized to unit length on actor creation.
        """
    @axis.setter
    def axis(self, value: Real3Like) -> None: ...
    friction: ArticulatedJointFrictionParams
    """Joint friction parameters.

    Note:
        Ignored for :class:`FREE <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` and
        :class:`HARD <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` joints.
    """
    inertia: Optional[float]
    """Joint inertia coefficient. Units are [kg] for translation DoFs and [kg·m²] for
    rotation DoFs.

    Note:
        Default is zero joint inertia.

    Note:
        Ignored for :class:`FREE <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` and
        :class:`HARD <superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointType>` joints.
    """
    @property
    def min_limit(self) -> Optional[Real3]:
        """Minimum joint limits for each DoF. Units are [m] for translation DoFs and
        [rad]
        for rotation DoFs.

        For 1D joints, limits must be defined by multiplying the scalar min limits by
        the joint axis. For 3D joints, each component must define the limit along one of
        the axes of the joint.

        Note:
            The definition of joint limits for spherical joints may be complex, and it
            may be easier to model them as 3 co-located revolute joints.
        """
    @min_limit.setter
    def min_limit(self, value: Optional[Real3Like]) -> None: ...
    @property
    def max_limit(self) -> Optional[Real3]:
        """Maximum joint limits for each DoF. Units are [m] for translation DoFs and
        [rad]
        for rotation DoFs.

        For 1D joints, limits must be defined by multiplying the scalar max limits by
        the joint axis. For 3D joints, each component must define the limit along one of
        the axes of the joint.

        Note:
            The definition of joint limits for spherical joints may be complex, and it
            may be easier to model them as 3 co-located revolute joints.
        """
    @max_limit.setter
    def max_limit(self, value: Optional[Real3Like]) -> None: ...
    limit_stiffness: float
    """Stiffness coefficient [N/m or N·m/rad] for the joint limit constraints.

    Note:
        Ignored for joints without limits.
    """
    limit_damping: float
    """Damping coefficient [N·s/m or N·m·s/rad] for the joint limit constraints.

    Note:
        Ignored for joints without limits.
    """
    @overload
    def __init__(self) -> None: ...
    @overload
    def __init__(
        self,
        name: str = ...,
        type: ArticulatedJointType | int = ...,
        parent_link_from_joint: TransformRT = ...,
        axis: Real3Like = ...,
        friction: ArticulatedJointFrictionParams = ...,
        inertia: Optional[float] = ...,
        min_limit: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
        max_limit: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
        limit_stiffness: float = ...,
        limit_damping: float = ...,
    ) -> None: ...
    def __eq__(self, other: object) -> bool: ...
    def __ne__(self, other: object) -> bool: ...

class ArticulatedLinkParams:
    """Parameters describing a single rigid link within an articulated actor.

    Each link is a rigid body in the articulation's kinematic tree. Mirrors
    :class:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams` for the per-link rigid-body
    properties (shape, mass, inertia, contact), and adds tree-structure fields
    (:attr:`parent_link`, :attr:`parent_joint_from_link`). Pose and velocity at
    creation time come from the articulated body, not from per-link fields.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams`,
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedJointParams`,
        :class:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams`
    """
    name: str
    """Link local name.

    Note:
        Must be unique among links of the same articulated actor. For soft-skinned
        actors, it must also not collide with nested soft actor local names.

    Note:
        Must not contain forward slash, backslash, or embedded NUL characters, which
        are reserved for hierarchy paths or incompatible with actor path formatting.

    Note:
        If left empty, a unique default name (e.g., "link_0", "link_1", ...) is
        assigned automatically.

    Note:
        In the scene the corresponding actor is named
        "articulatedActorName/linkLocalName". If the articulated actor name is
        empty, link actors use "unnamed_articulation/linkLocalName".
    """
    parent_link: int
    """Index of the parent link in
    :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedActorParams.links`, or -1 for the root.

    Note:
        Links must be listed in parent-first order: ``parentLink < i`` for the i-th
        link.

    Note:
        The root link (index 0) must have ``parentLink == -1``.
    """
    parent_joint_from_link: TransformRT
    """Rotation and translation of the link with respect to the parent joint.

    Warning:
        The rotation must be identity. Non-identity rotations are not supported yet.
    """
    shape: ShapeHandle
    """Shape handle defining the actor's geometry and other metadata.

    Note:
        A shape can be shared by multiple actors, even actors in different scenes.

    Note:
        Dynamic links require a shape with a surface mesh when link contact is
        enabled. An articulated actor enables link contact when no skin shape is
        provided. A soft-skinned actor enables link contact when
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.SoftSkinnedActorParams.enable_colliding_links` is
        true.

    See Also:
        :class:`~superdex.physics.ShapeHandle`,
        :func:`~superdex.physics.load_shape_from_file`
    """
    layer: str
    """Contact layer name for filtering contacts between actors.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric`,
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric`
    """
    collider_type: ColliderType
    """Collision detection geometry.

    Note:
        Determines how OTHER actors detect contact with this actor. It does not
        affect how this actor detects contact with other actors.
    """
    contact: ContactParams
    """Contact mechanics parameters."""
    has_gravity: bool
    """If true, the link actor will be affected by gravity.

    See Also:
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.set_gravity`
    """
    density: Optional[float]
    """Uniform density [kg/m³] of the actor. Must be positive if provided.

    Note:
        Specify either density or mass, but not both.

    Note:
        If density is set, mass is computed automatically from volume (and vice
        versa).

    Note:
        If neither is set, :const:`~superdex.physics.DEFAULT_DENSITY` is used.

    See Also:
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedLinkParams.mass`
    """
    mass: Optional[float]
    """Total mass [kg] of the actor. Must be positive if provided.

    Note:
        Specify either mass or density, but not both.

    Note:
        If mass is set, density is computed automatically from volume (and vice
        versa).

    See Also:
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.ArticulatedLinkParams.density`
    """
    @property
    def center_of_mass(self) -> Optional[Real3]:
        """Position [m] of the center of mass in the link actor's local frame.

