                translational DoFs and [rad/s] for rotational DoFs. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_joint_velocities`
        """
    def set_articulated_pose_from_links(
        self,
        world_from_links: ArrayLikeTransformRT,
    ) -> None:
        """Set the pose of an articulated actor from the world-from-local link
        transforms.

        Args:
            world_from_links (ArrayLikeTransformRT): World-from-local link transforms.
                Must be of size equal to the number of links.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            Transforms are automatically projected onto valid joint space.

        Note:
            If the actor has a pose controller, its target pose is reset to the provided
            transforms and its target velocity is set to zero. Call
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_velocity` afterward to
            use a non-zero target velocity.

        Note:
            Does not affect the actor's velocities.

        Note:
            Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler
            in the first time step after this method is called.

        Warning:
            Round-trip error:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_pose_from_links` followed by
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_link_transforms` may not
            return identical values due to internal representation differences.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_pose_from_joints`
        """
    def set_articulated_pose_from_joints(self, pose: ArrayLikeReal) -> None:
        """Set the pose of an articulated actor from joint DoFs.

        Args:
            pose (ArrayLikeReal): Joint DoF values to set. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            If the actor has a pose controller, its target pose is reset to the provided
            pose and its target velocity is set to zero. Call
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_velocity` afterward to
            use a non-zero target velocity.

        Note:
            Does not affect the actor's velocities.

        Note:
            Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler
            in the first time step after this method is called.

        Warning:
            Round-trip error:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_pose_from_joints` followed by
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose` may not return
            identical values due to internal representation differences.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_pose_from_links`
        """
    def set_articulated_joint_velocities(self, velocities: ArrayLikeReal) -> None:
        """Set time derivatives of the articulated actor DoFs.

        Args:
            velocities (ArrayLikeReal): Joint DoF velocities to set. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            If the actor has a pose controller, target velocity is also set to the
            provided velocities.

        Note:
            Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler
            in the first time step after this method is called.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_joint_velocities`
        """
    def add_articulated_delta_to_pose(
        self,
        pose: ArrayLikeReal,
        delta_dofs: ArrayLikeReal,
        out_pose: ArrayLikeReal,
    ) -> None:
        """Add a pose delta to a pose using joint-aware composition.

        Args:
            pose (ArrayLikeReal): Base pose as joint DoFs. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.
            delta_dofs (ArrayLikeReal): Pose delta to add. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.
            out_pose (ArrayLikeReal): Output pose after adding deltaDofs. Must be of
                size :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            Deltas cannot be simply added to poses. This function uses joint information
            to correctly add the delta.

        Note:
            Useful for adding time-stepped velocity to a reference pose.

        Note:
            For 3D rotations, delta values are interpreted as Lie-algebra
            rotation-vector increments.

        Note:
            For 3D rotations, angular velocity is not directly the time derivative of
            the rotation vector representation.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.compute_articulated_pose_delta`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose_distance`
        """
    def compute_articulated_pose_delta(
        self,
        pose_base: ArrayLikeReal,
        pose_target: ArrayLikeReal,
        out_delta_dofs: ArrayLikeReal,
    ) -> None:
        """Compute the pose delta from a base pose to a target pose.

        Args:
            pose_base (ArrayLikeReal): Base pose as joint DoFs. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.
            pose_target (ArrayLikeReal): Target pose as joint DoFs. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.
            out_delta_dofs (ArrayLikeReal): Pose delta. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            Deltas cannot be simply subtracted between poses. This function uses joint
            information to correctly subtract the delta.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.add_articulated_delta_to_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose_distance`
        """
    def get_articulated_pose_distance(
        self,
        pose_a: ArrayLikeReal,
        pose_b: ArrayLikeReal,
        out_trans_distances: ArrayLikeReal,
        out_rot_distances: ArrayLikeReal,
    ) -> None:
        """Compute per-joint distances between two poses.

        Args:
            pose_a (ArrayLikeReal): First pose as joint DoFs. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.
            pose_b (ArrayLikeReal): Second pose as joint DoFs. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.
            out_trans_distances (ArrayLikeReal): Translation distances [m] for each
                joint. Must be of size equal to the number of joints.
            out_rot_distances (ArrayLikeReal): Rotation distances [rad] for each joint.
                Must be of size equal to the number of joints.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            Uses joint-specific distance metrics (Euclidean for translation, angle for
            rotation).

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.add_articulated_delta_to_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.compute_articulated_pose_delta`
        """
    def has_articulated_pose_controller(self) -> bool:
        """Check if the articulated actor has a pose controller.

        Returns:
            True if a pose controller exists, false otherwise.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.add_articulated_pose_controller`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.remove_articulated_pose_controller`
        """
    def add_articulated_pose_controller(self, params: PoseControllerParams) -> None:
        """Add a pose controller to an articulated actor.

        Args:
            params (PoseControllerParams): Parameters defining the pose controller.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            Only one pose controller is allowed per actor. Adding a second controller
            raises an error.

        Note:
            The initial target pose and target velocity are set to the actor's current
            pose and velocity.

        Note:
            Empty tracking arrays are allowed. Default zero-gain parameters are used for
            any empty array.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.remove_articulated_pose_controller`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.has_articulated_pose_controller`
        """
    def remove_articulated_pose_controller(self) -> None:
        """Remove the pose controller.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors.

        Note:
            Returns an error if no pose controller exists.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.add_articulated_pose_controller`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.has_articulated_pose_controller`
        """
    def set_articulated_target_link_transforms(
        self,
        world_from_targets: ArrayLikeTransformRT,
    ) -> None:
        """Set the target pose for the controller expressed as link transforms.

        Args:
            world_from_targets (ArrayLikeTransformRT): Target world-from-link transforms
                to set. Must be of size equal to the number of links.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only supported for articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Also affects target velocity, which depends on how the target changes
            between simulation steps.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_pose`
        """
    def set_articulated_target_pose(self, pose: ArrayLikeReal) -> None:
        """Set the target pose for the controller expressed as joint DoFs.

        Args:
            pose (ArrayLikeReal): Target pose as joint DoFs to set. Must be of size
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Also affects target velocity, which depends on how the target changes
            between simulation steps.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_target_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_target_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_velocity`
        """
    def reset_articulated_target_link_transforms(
        self,
        world_from_targets: ArrayLikeTransformRT,
    ) -> None:
        """Reset the target pose of the controller expressed as link transforms.

        Args:
            world_from_targets (ArrayLikeTransformRT): Target world-from-link transforms
                to reset to. Must be finite and of size equal to the number of links.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Sets the target to the provided transforms and the target velocity to zero,
            so no velocity kick is introduced.

        Note:
            To use a non-zero target velocity, call
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_velocity` after this
            function.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_pose`
        """
    def reset_articulated_target_pose(self, pose: ArrayLikeReal) -> None:
        """Reset the target pose of the controller expressed as joint DoFs.

        Args:
            pose (ArrayLikeReal): Target pose as joint DoFs to reset to. Must be finite
                and of size :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Sets the target to the provided pose and the target velocity to zero, so no
            velocity kick is introduced.

        Note:
            To use a non-zero target velocity, call
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_velocity` after this
            function.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_link_transforms`
        """
    def set_articulated_target_velocity(self, velocity: ArrayLikeReal) -> None:
        """Set the target velocity of the controller expressed as joint velocities for
        the
        next simulation step.

        Args:
            velocity (ArrayLikeReal): Target DoF velocities to set. [m/s] for
                translational DoFs and [rad/s] for rotational DoFs. Must be finite and
                of size :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Does not change target pose.

        Note:
            The velocity override is applied once at the start of the next simulation
            step to compute damping, then cleared automatically. To maintain a constant
            target velocity, call this function before each step.

        Note:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_pose` and
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_link_transforms`
            overwrite any pending target velocity with zero. Call this function after
            reset to use a non-zero target velocity.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.reset_articulated_target_pose`
        """
    def get_articulated_pose_constraints(self) -> SpanConstPoseConstraintInfo:
        """Get the pose controller's constraints.

        Returns:
            Span of pose constraint information.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.PoseConstraintInfo`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose_controller_params`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_pose_controller_params`
        """
    def get_articulated_pose_controller_params(
        self,
        out_params: PoseControllerParams,
    ) -> None:
        """Get the pose controller's tracking parameters.

        Args:
            out_params (PoseControllerParams): Output tracking parameters grouped by
                constraint type
                (:attr:`~superdex.physics.PoseControllerParams.link_pos_tracking`,
                :attr:`~superdex.physics.PoseControllerParams.link_rot_tracking`,
                :attr:`~superdex.physics.PoseControllerParams.joint_tracking`). All
                three arrays are link-indexed and must be pre-sized to numLinks; they
                are not resized. Entries in
                :attr:`~superdex.physics.PoseControllerParams.joint_tracking` for links
                without a controllable joint are reported as zero gains.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose_constraints`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_pose_controller_params`
        """
    def set_articulated_pose_controller_params(
        self,
        params: PoseControllerParams,
    ) -> None:
        """Set the pose controller's tracking parameters.

        Args:
            params (PoseControllerParams): Tracking parameters grouped by constraint
                type. Each array must be empty, size 1 (broadcast to all links), or size
                numLinks (per-link). An empty array will broadcast using a
                default-constructed PoseTrackingParams (zero gains) to all links.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Setting zero stiffness and damping disables the constraint but does not
            destroy it.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose_controller_params`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_pose_constraints`
        """
    def get_articulated_target_pose(self, out_pose: ArrayLikeReal) -> None:
        """Get the last target pose set to the pose controller.

        Args:
            out_pose (ArrayLikeReal): Output span for the target pose as joint DoFs.
                Must be of size :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_target_link_transforms`
        """
    def get_articulated_target_link_transforms(
        self,
        out_world_from_targets: ArrayLikeTransformRT,
    ) -> None:
        """Get the last target pose set to the pose controller, expressed as link
        transforms.

        Args:
            out_world_from_targets (ArrayLikeTransformRT): Output span for the target
                world-from-link transforms. Must be of size equal to the number of
                links.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_pose`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.set_articulated_target_link_transforms`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_target_pose`
        """
    def get_articulated_controller_force(self) -> SpanConstReal:
        """Get the generalized forces applied by the pose controller on each joint DoF.

        Returns:
            Flattened generalized-force vector for each joint DoF. Size equals
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs`. Units are [N] for
            translational DoFs and [N·m] for rotational DoFs.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to articulated actors with a pose controller.

        Note:
            Requires registering :class:`ARTICULATED_CONTROLLER_FORCE
            <superdex.physics.QueryType>` before the simulation step. Results are
            available after the simulation step completes.

        Note:
            Requires the actor to support :class:`ARTICULATED_CONTROLLER_FORCE
            <superdex.physics.QueryType>`.

        Note:
            Equivalent to using :class:`CONSTRAINT_FORCE <superdex.physics.QueryType>`
            on each of the pose controller's constraints and projecting the constraint
            forces through the link Jacobians to joint DoF space (i.e., Σ Jᵢᵀ · fᵢ for
            each pose constraint i).

        Note:
            If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, the returned generalized
            forces may be stale.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.register_query`,
            :class:`ARTICULATED_CONTROLLER_FORCE <superdex.physics.QueryType>`
        """
    def is_nested_link_actor(self) -> bool:
        """Check if the actor is a rigid link within an articulated actor.

        Returns:
            True if the actor is a nested link actor, false otherwise.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_nested_link_actors`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_actor`
        """
    def is_nested_soft_actor(self) -> bool:
        """Check if the actor is a soft actor nested within a soft skinned articulated
        actor.

        Returns:
            True if the actor is a nested soft actor, false otherwise.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_nested_soft_actors`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_articulated_actor`
        """
    def get_articulated_actor(self) -> ActorHandle:
        """Get the owning articulated actor.

        Returns:
            Handle to the owning articulated actor.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to nested link or nested soft actors within articulated
            actors.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.is_nested_link_actor`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_nested_link_actors`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.is_nested_soft_actor`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_nested_soft_actors`
        """
    def get_articulated_jacobian(self) -> SpanConstReal:
        """Get the Jacobian with respect to the articulated DoFs in world frame.

        Returns:
            Jacobian matrix in row-major order with shape [6, numArticulatedDoFs], where
            6 is the number of rigid DoFs of the link (3 translation + 3 rotation) and
            numArticulatedDoFs is :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_num_dofs` of the
            owning articulated actor.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to nested link actors within articulated actors.

        Note:
            To get the Jacobian in the articulation's root frame, left-multiply the
            Jacobian by the 6×6 block-diagonal of the root-from-world rotation:

            ::

                [ R  0 ] · J
                [ 0  R ]

            where R is the 3×3 root-from-world rotation matrix (i.e., the transpose of
            the owning articulated actor's world-from-root rotation).

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.is_nested_link_actor`
        """

class Constraint:
    """Represents a constraint that restricts the degrees of freedom of one or more
    actors.

    Constraints enforce relationships between actor degrees of freedom (DoFs), such
    as fixing positions, limiting joint angles, or tracking target poses. They apply
    forces to maintain desired configurations using spring-damper mechanics
    controlled by stiffness and damping parameters.

    Note:
        Each constraint belongs to exactly one scene.

    Note:
        Each constraint acts on the degrees of freedom of one or more actors.

    Note:
        The type of constraint determines which methods are applicable.

    Warning:
        Concurrent access to a constraint is illegal.
    """
    def get_type(self) -> ConstraintType:
        """Get the type of the constraint.

        Returns:
            Type of the constraint.

        Note:
            Some methods are only valid for certain constraint types.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.ConstraintType`
        """
    def get_handle(self) -> ConstraintHandle:
        """Get the handle associated with this constraint.

        Returns:
            Handle to this constraint.

        Note:
            Handles are safe to store and remain valid throughout the constraint
            lifespan.

        Note:
            Call :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_constraint` to look up the
            constraint's pointer from the constraint's handle.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_constraint`
        """
    def get_stiffness(self) -> float:
        """Get the constraint's stiffness parameter.

        Returns:
            Stiffness value. [N/m] for translation constraints, [N·m/rad] for rotation
            constraints.

        Note:
            Higher stiffness results in stronger constraint forces/torques.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_stiffness`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_damping`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_saturation`
        """
    def set_stiffness(self, stiffness: float) -> None:
        """Set the constraint's stiffness parameter.

        Args:
            stiffness (float): Stiffness value. [N/m] for translation constraints,
                [N·m/rad] for rotation constraints. Must be non-negative and finite.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_stiffness`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_damping`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_saturation`
        """
    def get_damping(self) -> float:
        """Get the constraint's damping parameter.

        Returns:
            Damping value. [N·s/m] for translation constraints, [N·m·s/rad] for rotation
            constraints.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_damping`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_stiffness`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_saturation`
        """
    def set_damping(self, damping: float) -> None:
        """Set the constraint's damping parameter.

        Args:
            damping (float): Damping value. [N·s/m] for translation constraints,
                [N·m·s/rad] for rotation constraints. Must be non-negative and finite.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_damping`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_stiffness`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_saturation`
        """
    def get_saturation(self) -> float:
        """Get the constraint's saturation parameter.

        Returns:
            Saturation distance [m] for translation constraints or angle [rad] for
            rotation constraints, or a negative value if saturation is disabled.

        Note:
            A positive value smoothly limits the magnitude of the elastic (stiffness)
            contribution to stiffness * saturation. The damping contribution is separate
            and is not limited by saturation.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_saturation`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_stiffness`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_damping`
        """
    def set_saturation(self, saturation: float) -> None:
        """Set the constraint's saturation parameter.

        Args:
            saturation (float): Saturation distance [m] for translation constraints or
                angle [rad] for rotation constraints, or any negative value to disable
                saturation. Must be finite and non-zero.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            A positive value smoothly limits the magnitude of the elastic (stiffness)
            contribution to stiffness * saturation. The damping contribution is separate
            and is not limited by saturation.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_saturation`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_stiffness`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_damping`
        """
    def get_deviation(self) -> DynamicArrayReal:
        """Compute the constraint's current deviation from its target, limits, or
        coupling
        condition.

        Returns:
            Vector of constraint deviation values, one per constraint dimension. Units:
            [m] for translation constraints or [rad] for rotation constraints. Size
            equals the number of scalar constraint equations (e.g., 3 for
            position/rotation pivots and joints, 1 for single-DoF range/target
            constraints).

        Note:
            For constraints with targets: deviation is the distance/angle error from
            target.

        Note:
            For constraints with range limits: deviation indicates how far the current
            value is from the valid range.

        Note:
            For coupling constraints without a target or range: deviation is the
            constraint violation, i.e. how far the coupling is from being satisfied
            (zero when exactly satisfied).
        """
    def get_force(self) -> SpanConstReal:
        """Get the force/torque applied by the constraint.

        Values are ordered first by actor (in the order returned by
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_actor`), then by DoF within each actor
        (in the order returned by
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_dof_indices_for_actor`). Each entry has
        units conjugate to its DoF: [N] for translational DoFs and [N·m] for rotational
        DoFs (so a single returned vector may mix both, e.g. for
        :class:`RIGID_PIVOT_POSITION <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>` the 6 entries
        are 3 force [N] followed by 3 torque [N·m] components on the rigid actor).

        Returns:
            Flattened generalized-force vector. One entry per constrained DoF.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Requires registering :class:`CONSTRAINT_FORCE <superdex.physics.QueryType>`
            before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step
            completes.

        Note:
            If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, the returned force may
            be inaccurate.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.register_query`,
            :class:`CONSTRAINT_FORCE <superdex.physics.QueryType>`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_dof_indices_for_actor`
        """
    def get_num_actors(self) -> int:
        """Get the number of actors affected by the constraint.

        Returns:
            Number of actors affected by the constraint.
        """
    def get_actor(self, actor_index: int) -> Actor:
        """Get one of the actors affected by this constraint.

        Args:
            actor_index (int): Actor index in the range [0,
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_num_actors`).

        Returns:
            Pointer to the actor.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_num_actors`
        """
    def get_dof_indices_for_actor(self, actor_index: int) -> SpanConstInt:
        """Get the degrees of freedom (DoF) indices affected by this constraint on a
        specific actor.

        Args:
            actor_index (int): Actor index in the range [0,
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_num_actors`).

        Returns:
            Span of DoF indices for the specified actor.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_num_actors`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_actor`
        """
    def set_target_position(self, position: Real3Like) -> None:
        """Set the constraint's target position in world frame.

        Args:
            position (Real3Like): Target position [m] in world frame. Must be finite.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to position-target constraints: :class:`RIGID_PIVOT_POSITION
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, :class:`DEFORMABLE_NODE_POSITION
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, and :class:`RIGID_PIVOT_TO_RIGID_TARGET
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`. For :class:`RIGID_PIVOT_TO_RIGID_TARGET
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, this updates only the translation of the
            target center-of-mass transform.

        Note:
            Also affects target velocity, which depends on the difference between
            current and old target position.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_rotation`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_dof`
        """
    def set_target_rotation(self, rotation: QuaternionLike) -> None:
        """Set the constraint's target rotation.

        The target is interpreted according to the constraint type. For
        :class:`RIGID_PIVOT_ROTATION <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, it is the
        target pivot-frame rotation in world coordinates. For
        :class:`RIGID_PIVOT_TO_RIGID_TARGET <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, it is
        the rotation of the target center-of-mass transform in world coordinates. For
        :class:`ARTICULATED3D_ROTATION_TARGET <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, it is
        the target joint-local rotation. For :class:`JOINT_ROTATION_TRACKING
        <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, it is the target rotation of
        :attr:`~superdex.physics.JointRotationTrackingConstraintParams.actor_b` relative
        to :attr:`~superdex.physics.JointRotationTrackingConstraintParams.actor_a`. For
        :class:`ROD_ELEMENT_ROTATION_TO_RIGID <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`, it is
        the target rotation of the constrained rod element relative to the rigid actor.

        Args:
            rotation (QuaternionLike): Target rotation quaternion [x, y, z, w]. Must be
                finite and non-zero. Normalized before use.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Also affects target velocity, which depends on the difference between
            current and old target rotation.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_position`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_dof`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_ref_relative_rotation`
        """
    def set_target_dof(self, target: float) -> None:
        """Set the constraint's target DoF.

        Args:
            target (float): Target DoF value. Units: [m] for translation DoFs, [rad] for
                rotation DoFs.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to :class:`ARTICULATED_SINGLE_DOF_TARGET
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`.

        Note:
            Also affects target velocity, which depends on the difference between
            current and old target DoF.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_position`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_rotation`
        """
    def update_old_target(self) -> None:
        """Update the old target to match the current target.

        Call this method after changing a target discontinuously, and before stepping
        the scene, to prevent that change from contributing to damping during the next
        simulation step.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to constraints with a target.
        """
    def set_ref_relative_rotation(
        self,
        rotation_a: QuaternionLike,
        rotation_b: QuaternionLike,
    ) -> None:
        """Set a relative-rotation target from two rotations expressed in a common
        frame.

        Sets the target to inverse(``rotation_a``) * ``rotation_b``.

        Args:
            rotation_a (QuaternionLike): First rotation. Represents
                :attr:`~superdex.physics.JointRotationTrackingConstraintParams.actor_a`
                for :class:`JOINT_ROTATION_TRACKING <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`
                and the rigid actor for :class:`ROD_ELEMENT_ROTATION_TO_RIGID
                <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`. Must be finite and non-zero.
                Normalized before use.
            rotation_b (QuaternionLike): Second rotation. Represents
                :attr:`~superdex.physics.JointRotationTrackingConstraintParams.actor_b`
                for :class:`JOINT_ROTATION_TRACKING <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`
                and the selected rod element for :class:`ROD_ELEMENT_ROTATION_TO_RIGID
                <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`. Must be finite and non-zero.
                Normalized before use.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to :class:`JOINT_ROTATION_TRACKING
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>` and :class:`ROD_ELEMENT_ROTATION_TO_RIGID
            <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`.

        Note:
            Also affects target velocity, which depends on the difference between
            current and old target relative rotation.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.set_target_rotation`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.update_old_target`
        """
    def get_limit_min_values(self) -> SpanConstReal:
        """Get the constraint's minimum limit values.

        Returns:
            Span of minimum values for each constrained DoF. Units: [m] for translation
            DoFs, [rad] for rotation DoFs.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to range-based constraints
            (:class:`ARTICULATED_SINGLE_DOF_RANGE <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`,
            :class:`ARTICULATED3D_ROTATION_RANGE <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`,
            :class:`JOINT_ROTATION_RANGE <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`).

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_limit_max_values`
        """
    def get_limit_max_values(self) -> SpanConstReal:
        """Get the constraint's maximum limit values.

        Returns:
            Span of maximum values for each constrained DoF. Units: [m] for translation
            DoFs, [rad] for rotation DoFs.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Only applicable to range-based constraints
            (:class:`ARTICULATED_SINGLE_DOF_RANGE <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`,
            :class:`ARTICULATED3D_ROTATION_RANGE <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`,
            :class:`JOINT_ROTATION_RANGE <superdex.physics.ConstraintType>`).

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.get_limit_min_values`
        """
    def register_query(self, type: QueryType | int) -> QueryHandle:
        """Register a query to compute data for this constraint.

        Args:
            type (QueryType | int): Type of query to register.

        Returns:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.QueryHandle` for the registered query.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Queries may add substantial computational overhead. Use only when necessary.

        Note:
            Data becomes available after the next simulation step (even if the time-step
            is zero).

        Note:
            Call :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.cancel_query` when the query is not
            needed again in the future.

        Note:
            Queries are reference counted internally, so they will be available as long
            as there is one outstanding :class:`~superdex.physics.QueryHandle`.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.cancel_query`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.is_query_supported`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.register_query`
        """
    def cancel_query(self, handle: QueryHandle) -> None:
        """Cancel a previously registered query.

        Args:
            handle (QueryHandle): :class:`~superdex.physics.QueryHandle` from a previous
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.register_query` call.

        Note:
            Cancelling queries may improve memory usage and/or performance if the query
            is no longer needed.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.register_query`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.cancel_query`
        """
    def is_query_supported(self, type: QueryType | int) -> bool:
        """Check whether a query type is supported for this constraint.

        Args:
            type (QueryType | int): Type of query to check.

        Returns:
            True if :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.register_query` would succeed
            for this query type, false otherwise.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Constraint.register_query`
        """

class Scene:
    """Represents a simulation scene.

    Note:
        Each scene manages the simulation of a series of actors.

    Note:
        Actors from different scenes do not interact with each other.

    Warning:
        Concurrent access to the scene and its actors and constraints is illegal.
    """
    DEFAULT_CALLBACK_PRIORITY: int
    """Default priority for callback ordering. Lower values execute earlier (higher
    priority).
    """
    def get_handle(self) -> SceneHandle:
        """Get the scene handle.

        Returns:
            Scene's handle.

        Note:
            Handles are safe to store and remain valid throughout the scene lifespan.

        Note:
            Call :func:`~superdex.physics.get_scene` to look up the scene's pointer from
            the scene's handle.

        See Also:
            :func:`~superdex.physics.get_scene`
        """
    def get_name(self) -> str:
        """Get the name of the scene.

        Returns:
            Name of the scene.
        """
    def get_gravity(self) -> Real3:
        """Get the gravity vector in world frame.

        Returns:
            Gravity vector [m/s^2] in world frame.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.set_gravity`
        """
    def set_gravity(self, gravity: Real3Like) -> None:
        """Set the gravity vector in world frame.

        Args:
            gravity (Real3Like): Gravity vector [m/s^2] in world frame.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_gravity`
        """
    def get_solver_params(self) -> SolverParams:
        """Get the solver parameters.

        Returns:
            Current solver parameters.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.set_solver_params`
        """
    def set_solver_params(self, params: SolverParams) -> None:
        """Set the solver parameters.

        Args:
            params (SolverParams): Solver parameters to set.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_solver_params`,
            :class:`~superdex.physics.SolverParams`
        """
    def step(self, time_step_sec: float) -> None:
        """Advance the simulation of the :class:`~superdex.physics.Scene` one step.

        SuperDex Physics uses fully-implicit time integration, enabling substantially
        larger stable time steps than physics engines using explicit or semi-implicit
        methods, particularly for stiff systems. Fewer steps per simulated second often
        improve simulation performance and real-time factor.

        Args:
            time_step_sec (float): Time step size [s]. Must be non-negative.

        Note:
            Time steps of 10–25 ms (40–100 physics steps per simulated second) run
            robustly in most scenes, including complex contact-rich and deformable
            simulations. This is a practical starting range, not a guarantee. Smaller
            steps may still be required to resolve fast motion, accurately capture
            short-duration contact dynamics without excessive numerical dissipation,
            resolve dynamics associated with small geometric or discretization length
            scales, or improve nonlinear-solver convergence.

        Note:
            It is OK to use a different time step each time.

        Note:
            If the time step is zero, then the state of the simulation will not change,
            but pre-step and post-step callbacks will still be called, and queries will
            be updated.

        Note:
            If the time step is negative or NaN, no step is taken and an error is
            logged.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.IntegrationMethod`
        """
    def get_last_time_step(self) -> float:
        """Returns the time step size [s] from the most recent positive call to
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.step`.

        Returns:
            The time step size [s] from the most recent positive
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.step` call.

        Note:
            In a newly created scene, the return value is unspecified until the first
            positive :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.step` call.

        Note:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state` and
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state_from_bytes` restore this value
            from the captured state.

        Note:
            Calling :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.step` with a zero time step (e.g. to
            refresh queries without advancing the simulation) does not update this value
            (i.e. it retains the value from the last positive time step).
        """
    def get_total_simulation_time(self) -> float:
        """Returns the total simulation time [s] in the scene.

        Returns:
            The total simulation time [s].

        Note:
            May not match the real-time that has elapsed.
        """
    def get_solver_stats(self) -> SolverStats:
        """Get solver convergence metrics from the last simulation step.

        Returns:
            The :class:`~superdex.physics.SolverStats` from the last simulation step.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.SolverStats`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Actor.get_convergence_status`
        """
    def get_performance_stats(self) -> PerformanceStats:
        """Get timing and profiling metrics from the last simulation step.

        Returns:
            The :class:`~superdex.physics.PerformanceStats` from the last simulation
            step.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.PerformanceStats`
        """
    def set_force_single_island(self, force_single_island: bool) -> None:
        """Enables/disables forcing all actors in the scene to be in a single simulation
        island.

        An island is a group of actors and constraints that are solved together. Islands
        are managed automatically based on proximity and other factors. Islands can be
        solved in parallel, which can greatly improve the performance of the scene.
        However, if you suspect that island partitioning might be causing a problem,
        then you can use this function to force all actors in the scene to be simulated
        in a single island.

        Args:
            force_single_island (bool): Whether to force all actors to be in a single
                simulation island.

        Warning:
            Forcing single-island is a debugging feature. It will hurt performance.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_force_single_island`
        """
    def get_force_single_island(self) -> bool:
        """Get whether all actors are forced to be in a single simulation island.

        Returns:
            True if all actors are forced into a single simulation island.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.set_force_single_island`
        """
    def capture_state(self) -> StateHandle:
        """Capture the simulation state that changes from step to step for later
        restoration.

        Captured state includes actor solution, transforms, and velocities; current and
        previous constraint/controller targets; and external forces.

        Returns:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` to be used with
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state`. Call
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_state` or
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_all_states` when you're done with it.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Warning:
            Not supported for scenes with ROM actors.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_state`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_all_states`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_file`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_bytes`
        """
    def restore_state(self, handle: StateHandle, release_immediately: bool) -> None:
        """Restore captured simulation state. Optionally release the
        :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` at the same time.

        Args:
            handle (StateHandle): :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` from a
                successful call to :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`.
            release_immediately (bool): If true, release the state handle immediately
                (as if :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_state` were called), even
                if the restore fails.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            The :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` must have been captured from this
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Scene`.

        Note:
            The scene composition (actors, constraints) must be the same as when the
            state was captured.

        Warning:
            Does not create or destroy actors or constraints, or restore shapes,
            materials, or scene parameters. Captured mutable state on existing actors,
            including static actor transforms, is restored; if topology or persistent
            configuration changes, simulation results may differ.

        Warning:
            Restoration is not transactional. If restoration fails, the scene may be
            partially modified. Restore a known-good checkpoint or recreate the scene
            before continuing.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_state`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.release_all_states`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state_from_bytes`
        """
    def capture_state_to_bytes(self, out_data: ArrayLikeUint8) -> None:
        """Capture simulation state to a binary byte buffer.

        Captures the same simulation state as
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`, but writes the binary
        representation to caller-owned memory instead of storing it internally. This is
        useful for transferring state between processes or caching state outside the
        scene.

        Args:
            out_data (ArrayLikeUint8): Output byte buffer. Capture data is appended to
                the buffer.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            On failure, the output buffer may contain a partial capture. Discard the
            buffer or truncate it to its original size before reuse.

        Warning:
            Has the same capture restrictions as
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`, including no support for
            scenes with ROM actors.

        Warning:
            The binary representation uses an internal capture format. It is intended
            only for compatible scenes with the same actors and constraints created in
            the same order and the same component layouts, using the same SuperDex
            Physics build. It is not a stable long-term serialization or asset
            interchange format.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state_from_bytes`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_file`
        """
    def restore_state_from_bytes(self, data: ArrayLikeUint8) -> None:
        """Restore simulation state from a binary byte buffer produced by
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_bytes`.

        Args:
            data (ArrayLikeUint8): State data from a successful call to
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_bytes`.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            The byte buffer must have been captured from this or a compatible scene via
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_bytes`.

        Note:
            The capture and restore scenes must use the same SuperDex Physics build.

        Note:
            The restore requirements from :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state`
            apply, including scene composition (actors, constraints) being the same as
            when the state was captured.

        Warning:
            Has the same restore scope and non-transactional failure behavior as
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state`.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state_to_bytes`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.restore_state`
        """
    def release_state(self, handle: StateHandle) -> None:
        """Release a :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` when you are done with it.
        This
        frees up memory.

        Args:
            handle (StateHandle): :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` to release.

        Note:
            Redundant calls to ReleaseState will be ignored.
        """
    def release_all_states(self) -> None:
        """Release memory for all captured state and invalidate all prior
        :class:`~superdex.physics.StateHandle` objects.
        """
    def is_equal_state(self, state_a: StateHandle, state_b: StateHandle) -> bool:
        """Return true if both StateHandles are valid and refer to identical state
        information (full precision).

        Args:
            state_a (StateHandle): First StateHandle to compare
            state_b (StateHandle): Second StateHandle to compare

        Returns:
            True if both states are valid and identical.
        """
    def capture_state_to_file(self, file_path: str) -> None:
        """Captures a snapshot of the state of a :class:`~superdex.physics.Scene`,
        similar
        to :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`, then writes the data to a JSON
        file for manual inspection.

        Args:
            file_path (str): Path of the output file to write/overwrite (case sensitive
                on some filesystems).

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Warning:
            Not supported for scenes with ROM actors.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.capture_state`
        """
    @overload
    def create_rigid_actor(self, params: RigidActorParams) -> Optional[Actor]:
        """Create a rigid body actor.

        Args:
            params (RigidActorParams): Parameters defining the rigid actor.

        Returns:
            Pointer to the created :class:`~superdex.physics.Actor`, or None on error.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.RigidActorParams`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.destroy_actor`
        """
    @overload
    def create_rigid_actor(
        self,
        name: str = ...,
        layer: str = ...,
        shape: ShapeHandle = ...,
        world_from_local: TransformRT = ...,
        collider_type: ColliderType | int = ...,
        is_static: bool = ...,
        contact: ContactParams = ...,
        sdf: GridSdfParams = ...,
        has_gravity: bool = ...,
        density: Optional[float] = ...,
        mass: Optional[float] = ...,
        center_of_mass: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
        moment_of_inertia: Optional[Real6Like] = ...,
        boundary_element_type: ActorBoundaryElementType | int = ...,
        boundary_subsampling: Optional[BoundarySubsamplingParams] = ...,
        linear_velocity: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
        angular_velocity: Optional[Real3Like] = ...,
    ) -> Optional[Actor]: ...
    @overload
    def create_soft_actor(self, params: SoftActorParams) -> Optional[Actor]:
