            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.create_articulated_actor` (e.g. articulated
            joint limits).
        """
    def for_each_constraint(self, callback: Callable[[Constraint], None]) -> None:
        """Iterate over all the constraints in the scene using a callback.

        Args:
            callback (Callable[[Constraint], None]): Function called once for each
                constraint.

        Note:
            Includes constraints created implicitly by
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.create_articulated_actor` (e.g. articulated
            joint limits).

        Warning:
            Destroying other constraints or actors from within the callback is illegal.
        """
    def get_debug_draw(self) -> DebugDraw:
        """Get the debug draw interface for this scene.

        Returns:
            Reference to the :class:`~superdex.physics.DebugDraw` interface.

        See Also:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.DebugDraw`
        """
    def update_debugger(self) -> None:
        """This gives the debugger a chance to process messages that require reading or
        writing scene state.

        Please call this periodically if you are not actively stepping the scene. If
        this function is never called and the scene is never stepped, then some debugger
        features will not work.

        Note:
            Must be called on the scene's owning thread (like other
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Scene` methods).
        """
    def is_recording(self) -> bool:
        """Check if the scene is currently recording.

        Returns:
            True if recording is active, false otherwise.

        Note:
            A recording write failure does not end the recording session.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.start_recording`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.stop_recording`
        """
    def start_recording(self, file_path: str, params: RecordingParams) -> None:
        """Create or replace the specified file and start recording the scene to an HDF5
        file.

        Args:
            file_path (str): Path to the output recording file (case sensitive on some
                filesystems). File will be created or replaced.
            params (RecordingParams): Parameters controlling what data to record.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Enabling additional recording features will generally increase the recording
            file size and degrade performance.

        Note:
            If the scene is already recording, the previous recording is stopped before
            starting the new one.

        Warning:
            Requires a build with HDF5 support.

        Warning:
            The recording system may undergo a substantial refactor to expand its
            capabilities. Its API and recorded file format may change in future
            releases.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.stop_recording`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.is_recording`,
            :class:`~superdex.physics.RecordingParams`
        """
    def stop_recording(self) -> None:
        """Stop recording the scene and close the recording file.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.start_recording`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.is_recording`
        """
    def enable_layer_contact_asymmetric(
        self,
        layer_a: str,
        layer_b: str,
        enable: bool,
    ) -> None:
        """Enable or disable collision detection for an ordered pair of contact layer
        names. Order matters: controls only the specified direction (actors in layerA
        checking against actors in layerB).

        Args:
            layer_a (str): Name of the layer of the "colliding" actor (the one checking
                for contact). Must be non-empty.
            layer_b (str): Name of the layer of the "collider" actor (the one with a
                :class:`~superdex.physics.ColliderType` being tested). Must be
                non-empty.
            enable (bool): True to enable contact, false to disable it.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Contact is enabled by default. You only need to call this method if you wish
            to disable (or re-enable) contact for a specific layer pair.

        Note:
            Both layer-to-layer and actor-to-actor contact must be enabled for contact
            to occur.

        Note:
            Call twice with swapped arguments or use
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric` to affect
            collision checks in both directions.

        Note:
            Calling this method with a layer name not previously seen in the scene
            registers it as a new contact layer, increasing
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_num_contact_layers` and adding the name
            to :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enumerate_contact_layer_names`.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.is_layer_contact_enabled`
        """
    def enable_layer_contact_symmetric(
        self,
        layer_a: str,
        layer_b: str,
        enable: bool,
    ) -> None:
        """Equivalent to calling
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric` with ``layer_a``
        and ``layer_b`` in both orders.

        Args:
            layer_a (str): Name of the first contact layer. Must be non-empty.
            layer_b (str): Name of the second contact layer. Must be non-empty.
            enable (bool): True to enable contact, false to disable it.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.is_layer_contact_enabled`
        """
    def is_layer_contact_enabled(self, layer_a: str, layer_b: str) -> bool:
        """Check if collision detection is enabled for an ordered pair of contact layer
        names. Order matters: refers only to the specified direction (actors in layerA
        checking against actors in layerB).

        Args:
            layer_a (str): Name of the layer of the "colliding" actor (the one checking
                for contact).
            layer_b (str): Name of the layer of the "collider" actor (the one with a
                :class:`~superdex.physics.ColliderType` being tested).

        Returns:
            True if layer-to-layer contact is enabled, false if layer-to-layer contact
            is disabled.

        Note:
            Contact is enabled by default, so you will get true for any pair of layers
            unless overridden via
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric` or
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`.

        Note:
            This only checks the layer filter. Actor-to-actor contact can still be
            disabled with
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric` or
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric`.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`
        """
    def get_num_contact_layers(self) -> int:
        """Get the number of unique contact layer names in the scene.

        Returns:
            Number of unique layer names in the scene.

        Note:
            The count may include layer names not currently assigned to an actor.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enumerate_contact_layer_names`
        """
    def enumerate_contact_layer_names(self, callback: Callable[[str], None]) -> None:
        """Enumerate all unique contact layer names in the scene.

        Args:
            callback (Callable[[str], None]): Function called once for each layer name.

        Note:
            The callback fires :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_num_contact_layers`
            times.

        Note:
            Enumeration order is unspecified.

        Warning:
            Do not register new contact layers from inside the callback. Doing so may
            invalidate the enumeration and cause undefined behavior.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.get_num_contact_layers`
        """
    def enable_actor_contact_asymmetric(
        self,
        colliding: ActorHandle,
        collider: ActorHandle,
        enable: bool,
        include_nested_actors: IncludeNestedActors | int,
    ) -> None:
        """Enable or disable collision detection between two actors. Order matters:
        controls only the specified direction (colliding actor checking against collider
        actor).

        Args:
            colliding (ActorHandle): Handle of the colliding actor.
            collider (ActorHandle): Handle of the collider actor.
            enable (bool): True to enable contact, false to disable it.
            include_nested_actors (IncludeNestedActors | int): Whether nested actors
                should be affected by this contact setting. With :class:`NO
                <superdex.physics.IncludeNestedActors>`, only the exact handles are
                affected. With :class:`YES <superdex.physics.IncludeNestedActors>`,
                parent actors with nested actors resolve to the parent plus nested
                actors. The setting is applied to every ordered pair in the
                cross-product of the two resolved handle sets; no pairs outside that
                cross-product are affected. If the resolved sets overlap, pairs in the
                overlap, including self-pairs, are affected.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        Note:
            Contact is enabled by default. You only need to call this method if you wish
            to disable (or re-enable) contact for a specific actor pair.

        Note:
            Both layer-to-layer and actor-to-actor contact must be enabled for contact
            to occur.

        Note:
            Contact between adjacent links is automatically disabled when an articulated
            or soft-skinned actor is created. A later actor-contact setting can override
            that automatic disable for any pair included in the resolved actor sets. In
            particular, enabling contact between a parent actor and itself with
            :class:`YES <superdex.physics.IncludeNestedActors>` enables contact between
            that parent's nested actors, including adjacent links, unless a later
            actor-contact setting disables those pairs again.

        Note:
            Call twice with swapped arguments or use
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric` to affect
            collision checks in both directions.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_symmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_asymmetric`
        """
    def enable_actor_contact_symmetric(
        self,
        actor_a: ActorHandle,
        actor_b: ActorHandle,
        enable: bool,
        include_nested_actors: IncludeNestedActors | int,
    ) -> None:
        """Equivalent to calling
        :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric` with ``actor_a``
        and ``actor_b`` in both orders using the same ``include_nested_actors``.

        Args:
            actor_a (ActorHandle): Handle of the first actor.
            actor_b (ActorHandle): Handle of the second actor.
            enable (bool): True to enable contact, false to disable it.
            include_nested_actors (IncludeNestedActors | int): Whether nested actors
                should be affected by this contact setting. See
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric` for
                details.

        Raises:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.Error`: If an error occurs.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_actor_contact_asymmetric`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.enable_layer_contact_symmetric`
        """
    def register_pre_step_callback(
        self,
        debug_name: str,
        callback: Callable[[StepInfo], None],
        priority: int = ...,
    ) -> CallbackHandle:
        """Register a callback to execute before each simulation step.

        Args:
            debug_name (str): Descriptive name for debugging and profiling.
            callback (Callable[[StepInfo], None]): Callback function receiving
                :class:`~superdex.physics.StepInfo`.
            priority (int): Execution order. Lower values execute first (higher
                priority).

        Returns:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.CallbackHandle` for the registered callback.

        Note:
            Callbacks run sequentially on the thread that calls
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.step`, in increasing priority order (lower
            values first).

        Note:
            The relative order of callbacks registered with equal priority is
            unspecified. Assign distinct priorities when ordering matters.

        Note:
            Callbacks must be thread-safe if they access shared state.

        Note:
            Callbacks should not modify scene structure (add/remove actors/constraints).

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.cancel_callback`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.register_post_step_callback`
        """
    def register_post_step_callback(
        self,
        debug_name: str,
        callback: Callable[[StepInfo], None],
        priority: int = ...,
    ) -> CallbackHandle:
        """Register a callback to execute after each simulation step.

        Args:
            debug_name (str): Descriptive name for debugging and profiling.
            callback (Callable[[StepInfo], None]): Callback function receiving
                :class:`~superdex.physics.StepInfo`.
            priority (int): Execution order. Lower values execute first (higher
                priority).

        Returns:
            :class:`~superdex.physics.CallbackHandle` for the registered callback.

        Note:
            Callbacks run sequentially on the thread that calls
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.step`, in increasing priority order (lower
            values first).

        Note:
            The relative order of callbacks registered with equal priority is
            unspecified. Assign distinct priorities when ordering matters.

        Note:
            Callbacks must be thread-safe if they access shared state.

        Note:
            Callbacks should not modify scene structure (add/remove actors/constraints).

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.cancel_callback`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.register_pre_step_callback`
        """
    def cancel_callback(self, handle: CallbackHandle) -> None:
        """Cancel a previously registered callback.

        Args:
            handle (CallbackHandle): :class:`~superdex.physics.CallbackHandle` from
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.register_pre_step_callback` or
                :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.register_post_step_callback`. Must be
                owned by this scene.

        Note:
            Invalid and already-cancelled handles are ignored.

        See Also:
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.register_pre_step_callback`,
            :meth:`~superdex.physics.Scene.register_post_step_callback`
        """

